  "messages": [
    {
      "id": "1570251786629947442",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-12T01:39:59.8+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "Hi all, we're looking at on-die eFuse (device identity, anti-rollback, lifecycle bits) for a future GF180 design. We found egorxe's gf180_efuse_compiler and the TillitisZedulo eFuse + SRAM test chip on Run 1, but no bring-up data yet. Does anyone (Egor / the Zedulo team?) have results to share?\n\n1. Programming: what voltage/current/pulse did you use, and does it need a dedicated higher-voltage supply pad or does it run from the normal rails?\n2. Yield and read margin: programmed vs unprogrammed resistance spread, and any bits that failed to blow or read wrong?\n3. Any retention or bake data after programming?\n4. For wafer.space runs: is eFuse fine to include as-is (no extra layer, mask option or approval needed)?\n\nHappy to share whatever we learn on our side. Thanks!",
      "author": {
        "id": "1557575379156213927",
        "name": "0xaef",
        "discriminator": "0000",
        "nickname": "Agenxy",
        "color": null,
        "isBot": false,
        "roles": [],
        "avatarUrl": "2026-11_media/3d02d2c1593ba363a502a1e673af460b-E9B0A.png"
      },
      "attachments": [],
      "embeds": [],
